{"blocked-by-it-admin-cant-open-app-android":[{"type":"image","src":"https://faq.miniorange.in/wp-content/uploads/sites/10/2024/04/contact-us-admin-mdm.webp","alt":"contact us admin mdm","height":503},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"You might see this notice for any/all of the following reasons:","marks":["bold"]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Check if you are out of your office hours. Your IT Admin might have enabled the time-based restriction on work apps so that the apps can’t be used after working hours."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Your IT admin might have enabled some restrictions on the given app, e.g., the camera disabled."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Check if you have set the work profile password (in case of BYOD devices) and device password (in case of company-owned devices) as per the given password complexity rules. Try setting a strong password and check again."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Your device might not be compatible with the policy that the IT admin has enforced, e.g. runtime permission might be supported by Android version 12 but you have Android 11, the password is not set as per the complexity rules which are enforced, etc."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"If you have verified all these options above and have everything in place, you can now reach out to your "},{"t":"text","v":"IT administrator","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":" for the actual reason and get this fixed."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Android Mobile Device Management (MDM) Solutions by miniOrange can give you a clearer way to manage app permissions, device policies, and compliance requirements. It provides transparent visibility into configurations and enforcement status, helping admins quickly identify issues and keep devices operating smoothly. Learn more about "},{"t":"link","href":"https://www.miniorange.in/uem/mobile-device-management/android-mdm-solution?referer=https://faq.miniorange.in/knowledgebase/blocked-by-it-admin-cant-open-app-android","children":[{"t":"text","v":"Android MDM solution","marks":["bold"]}]},{"t":"text","v":"."}]}],"how-to-remove-work-profile-from-android-devices":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Want to remove the Work Profile from your Android device? Or facing the \"Can't Add Work Profile\" error?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Follow these quick steps to fix this instantly:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Open "},{"t":"text","v":"Settings","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":" on the device, then go to "},{"t":"text","v":"Accounts or Users & accounts","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":"."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Select the "},{"t":"text","v":"Work tab","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":" and scroll down to locate the "},{"t":"text","v":"Remove Work Profile","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":" option."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"When the confirmation prompt appears, tap "},{"t":"text","v":"Delete","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":"."}]}]]},{"type":"heading","level":4,"content":[{"t":"text","v":"For Motorola Edge Devices"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Open "},{"t":"text","v":"Settings","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":" on your Motorola Edge device and go to "},{"t":"text","v":"Passwords, Passkeys & accounts","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":"."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Tap on the "},{"t":"text","v":"Work tab","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":", and then click on "},{"t":"text","v":"Remove Work Profile","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":"."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"When prompted, tap "},{"t":"text","v":"Delete","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":" to confirm."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Once completed, the device will then delete all data associated with the work profile, including apps, settings, and any work-related information stored on it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Note:","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":" If you're still getting issues, contact us at "},{"t":"link","href":"mailto:mdmsupport@xecurify.com","children":[{"t":"text","v":"mdmsupport@xecurify.com"}]},{"t":"text","v":" for support."}]}],"how-to-reset-company-owned-devices-for-new-enrollment":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"The reset option is not available on company-owned devices because it is controlled by device management (MDM). To reset the device for new enrollment, follow the steps below:"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Steps to reset the device:","marks":["bold"]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Log in to the "},{"t":"link","href":"https://www.endpointdefence.com/dashboard","children":[{"t":"text","v":"miniOrange UEM dashboard"}]},{"t":"text","v":" and follow the steps below:"}]},{"type":"heading","level":4,"content":[{"t":"text","v":"Option 1: Deprovision the device (Recommended)"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Go to "},{"t":"text","v":"Device Inventory → Devices → Android","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":" and view the list of devices."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Search for the device using its serial number and click on the "},{"t":"text","v":"actions button (⋮)","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":" next to the device."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Click on the "},{"t":"text","v":"Deprovision","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":" option."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"The device will reset automatically and be ready for new enrollment."}]}]]},{"type":"image","src":"http://faq.miniorange.in/wp-content/uploads/sites/10/2026/04/device-deprovision.webp","alt":"Deprovision device from Android device inventory in miniOrange UEM dashboard"},{"type":"heading","level":4,"content":[{"t":"text","v":"Option 2: Enable reset from policy"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Go to "},{"t":"text","v":"Device Policies → Android → Policies","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":"."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Select the policy applied to the device and click on the "},{"t":"text","v":"actions button (⋮)","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":"."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Click "},{"t":"text","v":"Clone","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":", provide the required details, and click the "},{"t":"text","v":"Clone","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":" button."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Locate the cloned policy, click on the "},{"t":"text","v":"actions button(⋮)","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":", and select "},{"t":"text","v":"Edit","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":"."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Navigate to the "},{"t":"text","v":"Security","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":" tab. Locate the "},{"t":"text","v":"Factory Reset","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":" option, set it to "},{"t":"text","v":"Allow","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":", and click "},{"t":"text","v":"Submit","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":"."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Go to "},{"t":"text","v":"Device Groups → Android","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":" and click on "},{"t":"text","v":"Add Device Group","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":"."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"In the "},{"t":"text","v":"Create Android Device Group","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":" window, enter the "},{"t":"text","v":"Group Name","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":", "},{"t":"text","v":"Description","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":", and select the "},{"t":"text","v":"cloned policy","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":". Click "},{"t":"text","v":"Next","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":"."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"In the "},{"t":"text","v":"Associated Devices","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":" tab, select the device you want to reset and click "},{"t":"text","v":"Submit","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":"."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"This setting enables users to perform a factory reset from the device settings without impacting devices associated with the original policy."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"After completing the above steps, you will see the "},{"t":"text","v":"Factory Reset","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":" option on the device in the system settings, allowing you to reset the device when required."}]}],"g-suite-not-supported-managed-google-play-accounts-android":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"This notice occurs when you are trying to register the Android Enterprise with your corporate account "},{"t":"text","v":"(example@organization.com)","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":" which is not supported."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Please "},{"t":"text","v":"use a Gmail account","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":" for the same "},{"t":"text","v":"(example@gmail.com)","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":". "},{"t":"br"},{"t":"text","v":" It is recommended that you create a separate Gmail (@gmail.com) account for this registration that you can maintain for the entire organization."}]},{"type":"image","src":"https://faq.miniorange.in/wp-content/uploads/sites/10/2024/04/bring-android-work-accounts.webp","alt":"BYOD bring android work"},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Please feel free to contact us at "},{"t":"link","href":"mailto:mdmsupport@xecurify.com","children":[{"t":"text","v":"mdmsupport@xecurify.com"}]},{"t":"text","v":"."}]}],"how-to-ensure-work-apps-data-not-shared-to-personal-apps-on-byod-enrollments":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Multiple settings in the policy configuration will help you to ensure the prevention of sharing work data in the personal container."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Go to "},{"t":"text","v":"miniOrange MDM dashboard","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":" -> "},{"t":"text","v":"Android","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":" -> "},{"t":"text","v":"Policies","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":" -> Select your policy -> "},{"t":"text","v":"Data Sharing.","marks":["bold"]}]},{"type":"image","src":"https://faq.miniorange.in/wp-content/uploads/sites/10/2024/04/usb-data-access-transfer-mdm.webp","alt":"usb-data-transfer-mdm"},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"This screen will give you all the possible options that you can set up to ensure data transfer prevention."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"E.g.","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":" Set Copy Paste to option ‘"},{"t":"text","v":"Deny work to personal","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":"’ so any content copied from the work apps can’t be pasted in the personal container apps."}]}],"why-android-device-enrollment-fails-due-to-network-blocking":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"The following error message frequently appears during the enrollment process:"}]},{"type":"image","src":"https://faq.miniorange.in/wp-content/uploads/sites/10/2026/04/enrollment-error-msg.webp","alt":"Error during Android MDM enrollment"},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Android device enrollment may fail when network restrictions block access to required services. Successful Android Enterprise enrollment depends on communication with Google Play, Android provisioning services, and your Mobile Device Management (MDM) platform."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"content":[{"t":"text","v":"Required Endpoints and Protocols"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Your network must allow access to the following:"}]},{"type":"table","rows":[[{"header":true,"content":[{"t":"text","v":"Category"}]},{"header":true,"content":[{"t":"text","v":"Endpoints to Whitelist"}]}],[{"header":false,"content":[{"t":"text","v":"Google Core Services","marks":["bold"]}]},{"header":false,"content":[{"t":"text","v":"*.google.com, *.googleapis.com, *.gstatic.com, *.gvt1.com"}]}],[{"header":false,"content":[{"t":"text","v":"Android / Play Services","marks":["bold"]}]},{"header":false,"content":[{"t":"text","v":"play.google.com"}]}],[{"header":false,"content":[{"t":"text","v":"MDM Server","marks":["bold"]}]},{"header":false,"content":[{"t":"link","href":"https://www.endpointdefence.com","children":[{"t":"text","v":"https://www.endpointdefence.com"}]}]}]]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"content":[{"t":"text","v":"How do I know if this is a network issue?"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"The device setup or enrollment process does not start"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"The setup freezes or gets stuck"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Managed applications fail to install"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"content":[{"t":"text","v":"How can I quickly test if the network is the problem?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Try enrolling the device using a mobile hotspot or an unrestricted external network. If enrollment works outside your corporate network, your firewall or proxy is blocking required services."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"content":[{"t":"text","v":"What should I do to fix this?"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Contact your IT or network administration team"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Whitelist all required Google, Android, and MDM endpoints listed above"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Ensure HTTPS traffic over port 443 is fully allowed"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Note:","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":" Android Enterprise relies heavily on Google Play services. Even minor restrictions on Google domains can prevent successful enrollment and device setup."}]}],"what-can-employer-see-on-android-work-profile":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"What IT ","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":"can","marks":["italic","bold"]},{"t":"text","v":" manage / see:","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":" the work profile container — the managed (work) apps, the data inside them, work app inventory, and compliance/security status of the work profile. IT can enforce passcode policies, restrict copy/paste between work and personal apps, and remotely wipe the work container if you leave the organization."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"What IT ","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":"cannot","marks":["italic","bold"]},{"t":"text","v":" see:","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":" your personal side. The organization has full management control of the work profile but has no visibility or access to the device's personal profile. That means your personal apps, photos, messages, browsing, and personal accounts are not visible to your employer, and a wipe of the work profile leaves your personal data untouched."}]}],"how-to-sync-iphone-with-mdm-without-internet-or-wifi":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"When Wi-Fi is blocked or restricted by an MDM policy such as kiosk mode, the iPhone may lose internet connectivity. Once the device is offline, it cannot communicate with the MDM server, which prevents new profiles, policies, and commands from being pushed."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"content":[{"t":"text","v":"Steps to Restore Connectivity"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Connect the iPhone to a Mac","marks":["bold"]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Use a "},{"t":"text","v":"USB cable","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":" to connect the iPhone to a Mac."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Enable Internet Sharing on the Mac","marks":["bold"]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"On the Mac, go to: "},{"t":"text","v":"System Settings → General → Sharing → Internet Sharing","marks":["italic","bold"]}]},{"type":"image","src":"https://faq.miniorange.in/wp-content/uploads/sites/10/2026/04/turn-on-internet.webp","alt":"Enable Internet Sharing on the Mac","width":40},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Configure the following:","marks":["bold"]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Share connection from: "},{"t":"text","v":"Wi-Fi or Ethernet","marks":["bold"]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"To computers using: "},{"t":"text","v":"iPhone USB","marks":["bold"]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Turn "},{"t":"text","v":"Internet Sharing ON","marks":["bold"]}]}]]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Verify Internet Access on the iPhone","marks":["bold"]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Once Internet Sharing is enabled, the iPhone should "},{"t":"text","v":"receive internet connectivity through the USB connection","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":"."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Allow the Device to Sync","marks":["bold"]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"After connectivity is restored:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"The iPhone will reconnect to the MDM server"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"From the admin dashboard, go to Device Actions and click "},{"t":"text","v":"Sync Device","marks":["bold"]}]}]]}]]}],"common-mdm-enrollment-issues-and-fixes":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Common MDM enrollment issues usually fall into network, configuration, permissions, or device compatibility problems. Here are the most frequent ones and how to resolve them:"}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"content":[{"t":"text","v":"1. Enrollment Fails or Gets Stuck"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Causes:","marks":["bold"]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Poor internet connectivity"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Incorrect enrollment URL or token"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Expired enrollment invitation"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Server connectivity issues"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Fixes:","marks":["bold"]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Ensure the device has stable Wi-Fi or mobile data"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Verify the enrollment URL and credentials"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Regenerate enrollment tokens if expired"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Check MDM server health and firewall rules"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"content":[{"t":"text","v":"2. Device Not Appearing in the MDM Console"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Causes:","marks":["bold"]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Device sync delay"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Push notification service issues"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Enrollment completed partially"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Fixes:","marks":["bold"]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Refresh or resync the device"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Re-enroll the device if necessary"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"content":[{"t":"text","v":"3. Profile Installation Errors"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Causes:","marks":["bold"]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"User denied permissions"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Existing management profile/work container conflict"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"OS restrictions"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Fixes:","marks":["bold"]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Remove old management profiles/work container"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Ensure required permissions are granted"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Update the device OS to a supported version"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"content":[{"t":"text","v":"4. Android Enterprise Enrollment Problems"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Causes:","marks":["bold"]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Google Play services outdated"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Device not factory reset for fully managed mode"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Invalid QR code or token"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Fixes:","marks":["bold"]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Update Google Play Services"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Factory reset devices before enrollment if required"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Generate a fresh QR code or enrollment token"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"content":[{"t":"text","v":"5. Apple Device Enrollment Issues"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Causes:","marks":["bold"]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"APNs certificate expired"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Device not assigned in Apple Business Manager"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Activation lock enabled"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Fixes:","marks":["bold"]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Renew APNs' certificates before expiration"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Verify device assignment in Apple Business Manager"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Remove activation lock credentials if needed"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"content":[{"t":"text","v":"6. Policy or App Deployment Failures"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Causes:","marks":["bold"]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Device not compliant"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Insufficient storage"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Incorrect app licensing"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Fixes:","marks":["bold"]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Ensure the device meets compliance rules"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Free up storage space"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Verify app licenses and deployment settings"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"content":[{"t":"text","v":"7. Authentication Problems"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Causes:","marks":["bold"]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Incorrect user credentials"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"SSO or identity provider misconfiguration"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"MFA restrictions"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Fixes:","marks":["bold"]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Verify username/password"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Check Azure AD, Okta, or Google Workspace integration"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Confirm MFA policies support enrollment flows"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"content":[{"t":"text","v":"Best Practices to Prevent Enrollment Issues"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Keep devices updated"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Test enrollment workflows before mass deployment"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Use automated enrollment programs like Apple ADE or Android Zero-touch"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Monitor enrollment logs and audit reports"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Provide clear enrollment instructions to users"}]}]]}],"what-are-common-device-enrollment-issues-and-how-to-resolve-them":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"content":[{"t":"text","v":"1. What should I do if Gmail is not syncing in the Work Profile during enrollment?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"During device enrollment, you may see a prompt in the Gmail app asking you to click "},{"t":"text","v":"“Sync device”","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":", but the sync may not start. This usually happens when "},{"t":"text","v":"sync settings are disabled in the Work Profile","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"To resolve this issue:","marks":["bold"]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Open "},{"t":"text","v":"Settings","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":" on your device."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Go to "},{"t":"text","v":"Users & Accounts","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":"."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Select "},{"t":"text","v":"Work Profile","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":"."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Turn on "},{"t":"text","v":"Auto Sync (Work Data)","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":"."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Restart your device."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Once the device restarts, Gmail should begin "},{"t":"text","v":"syncing emails normally","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":" within the Work Profile."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"content":[{"t":"text","v":"2. What can cause device enrollment to fail in miniOrange MDM, and how can I fix it?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Device enrollment may fail or not complete due to "},{"t":"text","v":"existing Work Profiles, residual configurations, or cached data","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":" on the device."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Follow these steps to resolve the issue:","marks":["bold"]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Remove the existing "},{"t":"text","v":"Work Profile","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":" to prevent "},{"t":"text","v":"enrollment conflicts","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":"."},{"t":"br"},{"t":"text","v":" Go to: "},{"t":"text","v":"Settings → Accounts / Users & Accounts → Work Profile → Remove","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":", then delete the Work Profile."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Restart the device","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":" to clear "},{"t":"text","v":"temporary system issues","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":" affecting enrollment."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Clear the "},{"t":"text","v":"Google Play Services cache","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":" to remove "},{"t":"text","v":"corrupted or outdated data","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":"."},{"t":"br"},{"t":"text","v":" Go to: "},{"t":"text","v":"Settings → Apps → Google Play Services → Storage → Clear Cache","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":"."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Retry device enrollment","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":" by starting the "},{"t":"text","v":"enrollment process again","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":"."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"These steps help ensure a "},{"t":"text","v":"clean setup and successful enrollment","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":"."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"content":[{"t":"text","v":"3. Why are MDM policies not applied on the device after enrollment, and how can I fix it?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"In some cases, the "},{"t":"text","v":"latest policies from the MDM server may not be applied immediately","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":" after enrollment. This can result in "},{"t":"text","v":"missing configurations or restrictions","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":" on the device."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"To fix this, you can "},{"t":"text","v":"manually sync policies","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":" using the "},{"t":"text","v":"Sync Policies","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":" option."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Steps based on device type:","marks":["bold"]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Realme and Motorola devices:","marks":["bold"]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Open "},{"t":"text","v":"Settings","marks":["bold"]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Navigate to "},{"t":"text","v":"Security & Privacy","marks":["bold"]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Tap Your "},{"t":"text","v":"Work Policy Info","marks":["bold"]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Click the "},{"t":"text","v":"three-dot menu (⋮) ","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":"in the top-right corner"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Select Sync Policies","marks":["bold"]}]}]]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Samsung devices:","marks":["bold"]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Open "},{"t":"text","v":"Settings","marks":["bold"]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Navigate to "},{"t":"text","v":"Security & Privacy","marks":["bold"]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Tap "},{"t":"text","v":"Controls and Alerts","marks":["bold"]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Select Your "},{"t":"text","v":"Work Policy Info","marks":["bold"]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Click the "},{"t":"text","v":"three-dot menu (⋮)","marks":["bold"]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Select Sync Policies","marks":["bold"]}]}]]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Vivo devices:","marks":["bold"]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Open "},{"t":"text","v":"Settings","marks":["bold"]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Navigate to "},{"t":"text","v":"Security & Privacy","marks":["bold"]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Tap "},{"t":"text","v":"More Privacy Settings","marks":["bold"]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Select Your "},{"t":"text","v":"Work Policy ","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":">"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Click the "},{"t":"text","v":"three-dot menu (⋮)","marks":["bold"]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Select Sync Policies","marks":["bold"]}]}]]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"iQOO devices:","marks":["bold"]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Open "},{"t":"text","v":"Settings","marks":["bold"]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Navigate to "},{"t":"text","v":"Privacy Dashboards","marks":["bold"]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Select Your "},{"t":"text","v":"Work Policy Info","marks":["bold"]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Click the "},{"t":"text","v":"three-dot menu (⋮)","marks":["bold"]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Select Sync Policies","marks":["bold"]}]}]]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Manually syncing ensures the device receives and applies the "},{"t":"text","v":"latest MDM policies correctly","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":"."}]}],"what-data-can-employer-see-on-byod-device":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"On BYOD devices enrolled via miniOrange MDM, your employer's visibility is strictly limited to work-related data and device compliance information."}]}],"android-mdm-enrollment-failed":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"An Android device can fail to enroll in an MDM (Mobile Device Management) system for several reasons. The most common causes fall into these categories:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Network Connectivity Problems","marks":["bold"]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Device has no internet access."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Firewall, proxy, or VPN settings are blocking communication with the MDM server."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Weak or unstable Wi-Fi/mobile data connection."}]}]]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Device Compatibility Issues","marks":["bold"]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Android version is too old or unsupported by the MDM."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Device manufacturer restrictions interfere with enrollment."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"The device is rooted or running a custom ROM."}]}]]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Existing Device Management Configuration","marks":["bold"]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Device is already managed by another MDM."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"A work profile already exists and conflicts with the new enrollment."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Previous enrollment was not removed properly."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Residual MDM configurations from a prior enrollment remain on the device."}]}]]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Insufficient Device Storage","marks":["bold"]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"The device does not have enough free internal storage to install the MDM, create a work profile, or download required policies and applications."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Ensure the device has a minimum of "},{"t":"text","v":"10 GB of free internal storage","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":" available before attempting enrollment."}]}]]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Enrollment Method Issues","marks":["bold"]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"The QR code used for enrollment may be invalid or expired."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Zero-touch enrollment may not be properly assigned to the device."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Cached enrollment data may interfere with the enrollment process."}]}]]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Google Services Issues","marks":["bold"]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Google Play Services cache is corrupted or outdated."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Google Play Services are disabled or not functioning properly."}]}]]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"By verifying these items, most Android MDM enrollment issues can be identified and resolved successfully."}]}],"what-are-android-enterprise-device-enrollment-requirements":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"For enrolling Android devices in the miniOrange "},{"t":"link","href":"https://www.miniorange.com/uem/mobile-device-management","children":[{"t":"text","v":"Mobile Device Management (MDM) solution","marks":["bold"]}]},{"t":"text","v":", the following "},{"t":"text","v":"minimum Android Enterprise Recommended requirements","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":" must be met:"}]},{"type":"table","rows":[[{"header":true,"content":[{"t":"text","v":"Requirement"}]},{"header":true,"content":[{"t":"text","v":"Minimum Specification"}]}],[{"header":false,"content":[{"t":"text","v":"RAM","marks":["bold"]}]},{"header":false,"content":[{"t":"text","v":"At least "},{"t":"text","v":"4 GB","marks":["bold"]}]}],[{"header":false,"content":[{"t":"text","v":"Free Storage","marks":["bold"]}]},{"header":false,"content":[{"t":"text","v":"Minimum "},{"t":"text","v":"10 GB","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"text","v":" (may vary based on apps installed)"}]}],[{"header":false,"content":[{"t":"text","v":"Android Version","marks":["bold"]}]},{"header":false,"content":[{"t":"text","v":"Android 8.0+","marks":["bold"]}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"These requirements ensure smooth device enrollment, policy enforcement, and overall performance."}]}],"mdm-diagnostic-logs-windows-event-viewer":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"To view MDM diagnostic logs in Windows Event Viewer:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Press Win + R, type eventvwr.msc, and press Enter.","marks":["bold"]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Navigate to:","marks":["bold"]},{"t":"br"},{"t":"text","v":" "},{"t":"text","v":" Applications and Services Logs &rarr; Microsoft &rarr; Windows &rarr; DeviceManagement-Enterprise-Diagnostics-Provider","marks":["bold"]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Check Admin and Operational logs for policy sync, errors, and deployment status."}]}]]}],"how-to-enroll-ios-devices-apple-business-manager-mdm":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"To enroll iPhones and iPads in MDM through Apple Business Manager (ABM), the recommended approach is Automated Device Enrollment (ADE)."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"content":[{"t":"text","v":"Prerequisites"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"An active Apple Business Manager account."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"A supported MDM solution (such as Miniorange MDM)."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Apple devices purchased through Apple, an authorized reseller, or a carrier linked to your ABM account; alternatively, devices can be added later using Apple Configurator."}]}]]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"content":[{"t":"text","v":"Step 1: Connect Apple Business Manager to Your MDM"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"In ABM:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Sign in as an Administrator."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Go to Devices → Device Management Settings (or equivalent menu)."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Create a new MDM server entry."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Download the public key from the miniOrange MDM platform."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Upload the public key to ABM."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Download the server token from ABM and upload it to miniOrange MDM."}]}]]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"content":[{"t":"text","v":"Step 2: Add Devices to Apple Business Manager"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"There are two common methods:"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Automatic assignment"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Purchase devices from Apple or an authorized reseller linked to your ABM account."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Devices automatically appear in ABM inventory."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Manual addition"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Use Apple Configurator on a Mac or iPhone to add existing devices that were not originally purchased through ABM."}]}]]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"content":[{"t":"text","v":"Step 3: Assign Devices to the MDM Server"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"In ABM:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Open Devices."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Search for the serial numbers or order numbers."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Select the devices."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Choose Assign to Server."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Select your miniOrange MDM server."}]}]]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"content":[{"t":"text","v":"Step 4: Sync Devices into the MDM Platform"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"In your MDM console:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Sync with Apple Business Manager."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Confirm the assigned devices appear in the enrollment list."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Create an Automated Device Enrollment profile."}]}]]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"content":[{"t":"text","v":"Step 5: Enroll the Device"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"For a new or factory-reset iPhone/iPad:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Power on the device."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Connect to Wi-Fi or cellular data."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Complete the initial setup."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"The device contacts Apple activation servers."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Apple detects the ABM assignment and displays a Remote Management screen."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"The device automatically enrolls into your MDM and receives policies, apps, and configurations."}]}]]}],"which-devices-or-os-work-with-mdm-solution":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"miniOrange MDM platform supports a broad range of devices across major operating systems to ensure comprehensive enrollment and management capabilities."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Apple Devices","marks":["bold"]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"iOS 15.0 and later (iPhone)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"iPadOS 15.0 and later (iPad)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"macOS 11 (Big Sur) and later"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Android Devices","marks":["bold"]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Android 9.0 (Pie) and later for full Android Enterprise support."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Supported OEMs include Samsung, Google Pixel, OnePlus, Motorola, Xiaomi, Sony, LG, and Zebra. For a detailed list,"},{"t":"link","href":"https://androidenterprisepartners.withgoogle.com/devices/","children":[{"t":"text","v":"click here"}]},{"t":"text","v":"."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Zebra and Honeywell rugged devices are supported for warehouse and field use cases."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Windows Devices","marks":["bold"]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Windows 11 (PRO and Enterprise edition)"}]}]]}]}
